# Served verbatim artifacts are the ARTIFACT, not our formatting. Their own
# line-internal whitespace — tabs, space-before-tab, whatever the 1991 poster's
# own editor left behind — is part of the document and is never "fixed."
# CLAUDE.md invariant 4 forbids touching a served document's own words; this
# turns off git's whitespace-error checks for exactly those paths so the
# pre-commit hook's `git diff --cached --check` cannot demand an edit the law
# forbids. (Added 2026-09-02 by the Summit of E-Wrestling accession, whose
# usenet bodies are the first served documents in the collection to carry
# space-before-tab indentation of their own.)
promotions/*/archive/*.html -whitespace
promotions/*/rp/*.html -whitespace

# Their own ASCII rules are the ARTIFACT too. Usenet-era cards rule off their
# segments with runs of `=`, and a run of seven or more at the start of a line
# is exactly what `git diff --check` reports as a "leftover conflict marker" —
# which blocks the pre-commit hook on a document the law forbids editing. The
# WeWF's own Wrestling Spotlight segments open on `=======  WeWF Wrestling
# Spotlight ========`. Raising the marker size for served artifacts only turns
# off that false positive; real conflict markers in source and data files are
# still caught everywhere else. (Added 2026-09-02 by the WeWF enrichment
# accession, lot 0144.)
promotions/*/archive/*.html conflict-marker-size=99
promotions/*/rp/*.html conflict-marker-size=99

# The living pulse's public calendar (hook c100; the Janitor's D408/D412). RFC 5545 requires CRLF line endings, which
# `git diff --check` reads as trailing whitespace and which stopped preflight 301. The CR is the format, not our formatting.
# (Added 2026-10-06 by the coordinator.)
crawler/*.ics -text whitespace=cr-at-eol
